      "author": {
        "id": 1311150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T12:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "from the register map, this register description as follow:\nFOD REGISTERS (0X70 -\u003e 0X7F, 16-BYTES).\nThe FOD Registers are divided into 8 pairs. Each pair has one byte for gain setting, and one byte for offset setting. The first 6 pairs control the Received Power calculation for 6 power sectors during Power Transfer phase. The seventh pair calibrates the internal DC Load, and the eight pair is used during EPP Calibration Phase 1. The set values of the FOD Registers are found with the help of IDT developed calibration procedure using the nok9 tester. The FW initializes the FOD Registers from one of two sets default values, one for BPP mode, and one for EPP mode.\nThe correct set is loaded at completion of the ID \u0026 Configuration Phase. The AP may modify the registers at any time if needed to update the values.",
      "parentUuid": "ee58704a_59875c28",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 622,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 622,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "0987ac04cbd1c54029010cea6d0843ed1750ffcf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
